Z||000000||JSocha||05-21-2001||10:31 AM||||Well, yesterday my second of three girls graduated from High School and is off to the big "C" this fall.<P>Saturday afternoon for a family pre-graduation (and Heidi's belated B-Day party May, 15) get together, I fried over 30 pounds of chicken and I still have plenty left as most of my wife's family decided at last minute not to show.  <P>Ended up buying more chicken Friday morning just to cover all the people that "were" going to be coming at last minute and at the last minute they graciously called again to tell us they weren't going to be able to make it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Yesterday, got rid of more of the chicken, but now I have a meat tray, buns, chips and the other pan of chicken still left and we are going to be eating left overs for about a month!<P>Seems like only a few years ago I got married and now the kids are all grown up, graduatating and going on with their lives.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> &lt;sniff&gt; &lt;sniff&gt;<P>Next up is the youngest (who starts drivers ed today) who will be graduating in 4 years as she will be a Freshman in HS this fall.  Then, if Heidi does her four years straight of college, I will end up having two graduating at the same time.<P>I'm wondering if I should freeze all the left overs until then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or perhaps till they get married.<P>BTW, Heidi went out to her classes graduation party (first party she has been to in her life) with her older sister and got totally hammered in about 15 minutes off of Peach Tree Schnaps for the first time in her life.  <P>I just wish I could be home today just to see her praying to the monster bowl for the pounding monster in her head to go away.<P>Anybody out here want some left over fried chicken?  Just have to come on over is all!  Free food today...free beer tomorrow!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
