Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||01:19 PM||||Four year old frozen chicken - could be the start of a tradition.<P>My wife and I froze the top of our wedding cake ,and ate it for dessert on out 1st anniversary.<P> we were drink a bottle of Blue Nun wine (this was 20 years ago) and I was thinking - you know what would be great, to get about 50 or 60 bottles of this wine (we had it on our wedding nite too) and take it with us everywhere we go, and every year open a bottle on our anniversary.<P>  Debbie thought it was a neat idea. I thought about it for a few minutes, and added: then for that anniversary when there is only one of us left, that person can drink all the remaining bottles in one night.<P>   Debbie sat there for a minute and didnt say anything, then a tear started down one cheek. I said, whats the matter?<P>  and she said, "I'm gonna miss you!"<P>  (c:||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||05-22-2001||01:24 PM||||I don't envy you a bit. Three girls....I shudder at the very thought. If I had a daughter, she would never date. (Hey, I used to be a teenage guy, I know what we're like)<BR>A guy would come over to take my daughter out, and he and I would have an exchange something like this:<BR>Me: "So, taking my daughter out tonight. Tell me, do yo plan on trying to jump her bones?"<BR>At which point, her potential date would respond in one of two fashions:<BR><I>Fashion 1:</I> "why, no sir, I have too much respect for her to try that." To which of course, I would toss him out on his ass, because I don't want my daughter to date a liar.<BR><I>Fashion 2</I>"Well, yes sir, being a young man with my hormones in high gear, I have to admit, I probably will try that..." At which point, I'm gonna throw him out on his ass too cause, well, I don't need that sh*t!<BR>Ahhh...I love questions with no right answer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I have to say, you're handling your daughters' indescretion pretty well.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||JSocha||05-22-2001||02:43 PM||||To be honest, I told her to do it and get it out of her system now before she goes to college where I am sure she will eventually do it.  I try to keep the communciation lines open with them, so they can pretty much come to me about anything to which they have.  Unless of course it is more female to female talk...you know what I mean.<P>She is just to serious all the time and I felt as a teenager, she should have some fun and this is the time to do it especially before all her friends leave and go their separate ways.  Just to straight laced IMO.<P>Sadistic streak:  I'm a big guy, 5'11", long hair (down past my shoulders), 285 to 300 pounds with a strong martial arts and weightlifting background.<P>Anytime my daughters (actually step-daughters) bring home a date to introduce them to their mother and me, I say to their dates "Have her back by 10:00PM Sharp, not a millisecond after.  And if I find out you have touched her in an inappropriate manner which is not gentlemanly like, I'll bury you in little pieces and the authorities will be searching for your body forever not finding a trace".<P>Just to see the expression in their eyes and watch their jaws drop with the "Oh My God" tickling their little hormonal brains at this point is enough to make you laugh.<P>My oldest daughter, Wendy, when I did that to the first guy she brought home to meet her mom and me, he GULPED three times.  It was as funny as heck.<P>Ken, my wife did the wedding cake thing.  It actually tasted better after one year.<P>BTW, scientists have found which food actually causes women not to want to have sex anymore with their partners. --&gt; Wedding Cake!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-22-2001||03:40 PM||||the question to ask your daughters date is, "do you have any idea how precious my little girl is to me?"<P>  if he says yes or no, he's in the hot seat either way (my daughter is 19 now BTW).<P> I made it clear to my daughter, when she started dating, that someday she will be someones wife, and someday her date will be someones husband. And to keep that in mind, you most likely will not be his husband, so you are spending the evening with someone elses husband, and act like you are already married to someone else - and dont do anything that would not be appropriate for two married-to-other-people young adults to do. Dont so anything you wouldnt want your future husband to see or know about.<P>  puts it all into perspective nicely. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||05-22-2001||06:35 PM||||The 1st time my best friends daughter goes out on her 1st real date (she's only 12 now), her Dad and I have decided to sit on the front porch dressed in our best "down home" clothes (bib overalls, old boots, etc) with the matching shotguns in our hands (unloaded, of course but why tell her date that?).  My best friend's going to remind her date that she means alot to him and I'll sit quietly in the background just cocking my shotgun.  I think that should get the message across.  (And, yes.  I think of his daughter as my own.)<P>MM||||reg||1
